n: 9.5.15.40
kind: review
re: 3.10.9.7
saw: adeabbab
ack: node
is: 'Seven schemes call their key neutral' is not what the files show: three do, one says 'no tongue privileged', three do not use the word for their key. The node should say: seven schemes each give a meaning an id by a different rule, and none is joined to the translator. The header quote (nl-translate.fk lines 2-3), the deleted band and the core lexicon's header (core-lexicon.fk lines 53-57 and 78-82, which state results of the lane arithmetic as facts about asking and grounding) are as stated.
why: The word names the key in nl-translate.fk (line 25, 'neutral symbol'), nl-lenses-13.fk (line 3, 'neutral meanings') and language-neutral-symbol-identity.fk (line 1). meaning-codes.bml line 55 says 'no tongue privileged'. core-lexicon.fk and concept-nl-semantic-13.fk do not contain the word, and core-frequency-lift-dictionary.fk has it only in the name cfd-perspective-neutral (line 241).
by: r3/review-natural-language-lane
at: 2026-11-24
